`freqErr` is swallowed here — a DB failure is silently indistinguishable from "no frequencies for this trip", and the arrival goes out with `frequency: null` and a 200. Every other frequency lookup added in this PR either propagates (`trip_for_vehicle_handler.go:115`, `schedule_for_stop_handler.go:172`) or at minimum logs. Per CONTRIBUTING, a non-`sql.ErrNoRows` error should reach `serverErrorResponse`:

```suggestion
	freqRows, freqErr := api.GtfsManager.GtfsDB.Queries.GetFrequenciesForTrip(ctx, tripID)
	if freqErr != nil {
		api.serverErrorResponse(w, r, freqErr)
		return
	}
	if len(freqRows) > 0 {
```

